        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: AI news anchor brief\nTopic: real estate\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 12s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_M9H0DMX6MMJY2X5VXRR3Y8H2AH",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_S92WRSY63D989EP1264HGB01G0",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_JV995KX63HE7V7MDY65CJR4CHZ",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.71,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing an AI news anchor brief about real estate for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the AI news anchor brief \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a rack focus pulling from foreground occlusion to the subject on a 180mm long macro, framing with a tight crop that breaks the subject at the frame edge.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with a book light bounce producing an extremely soft wrap; grade as Eterna-style muted greens with gentle highlight roll-off. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. Emit one prompt, one paragraph, no framing text of any kind before or after it."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_06687CXBP6V9B2ZD6Y5ATVS6ZR",
        "kind": "image-input",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 700
        },
        "config": {
          "url": ""
        },
        "name": "Before image"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_C9WQNV4G2HCQX140TZJHKARAQK",
        "kind": "concat",
        "position": {
          "x": 350,
          "y": 520
        },
        "config": {
          "separator": "\n\n",
          "appendable_slots": {
            "parts": 2
          }
        },
        "name": "Brief joiner"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_2X4G23MK5PJ1SZAWFGJZR1PWRC",
        "kind": "text-input",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 980
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "TRANSFORMATION: [what changes]\nHOLD: [what must not change]"
        },
        "name": "Change contract"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_QV68R756128F3D6R0D2DY38NXZ",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 1050,
          "y": 700
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 900,
          "temperature": 0.75,
          "system_prompt": "You write the 'after' still prompt for an AI news anchor brief about real estate.\n\nThe attached before-image fixes framing, subject identity and camera position. Change ONLY what the change contract names; everything else \u2014 pose, crop, background geometry, focal length \u2014 stays identical so the reveal cuts cleanly.\n\nLight with an overcast soft dome with no directional shadow at all and grade to a filmic grade with halation on the specular highlights.\n\nReturn one prompt paragraph only.",
